# Single-page application fallback.
#
# Every path on this host shows the profile because the Angular router matches "**", but the static
# host answers an unknown path with its own 404 instead of booting the application. This rule
# (Cloudflare Pages, Cloudflare Workers with static assets and Netlify) rewrites every request that
# does not match a real file to index.html with a 200 status; real assets are still served from the
# bundle. A Worker that answers the request itself never applies these rules, so a bundle hosted on
# Cloudflare Workers also needs assets.not_found_handling = single-page-application in wrangler.jsonc
# (see README.md).
#
# Keep this file LF-only and free of a byte-order mark: the host parses it as plain text, and a
# carriage return after the status code leaves it unreadable, which silently drops the rule.
/*    /index.html   200